srt@aero.org (Scott "TCB" Turner) writes:

> I think the way to do this is: If your pet is
> faster than you are, and you try to move into
> your pet, then give the pet another move to get
> out of the way or exchange places with you ("your
> nimble cat darts past your ankles").

Well, there can be tame-monsters so big (dragons, trolls, etc.) that
it is impossible for them to exchange their position with you when you are in
a corridor. There must be some space to manouvre.
What about this one:
You step into your pet: attack/exchange-position/quit [a/e/q]

If you choose "exchange" then the pet, according to its size and speed,
can do:
- nothing (slow monsters, large ones in too little space, all -> random factor)
- exchange position (fast & little ones)
- step into an adiacent location (fast ones)
May be pets can be trained to exchange their position with you, giving them
food after they exchange places with you.
